
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  KimRity — Arch + Hyprland security workstation     │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Install to disk (WARNING: the disk will be wiped):

      bash /root/install.sh --disk /dev/vda --efi

  Default = lean (desktop + daily apps + Security Gate + kimscan).
  Optional, on purpose:
      --lab       analysis tools (metasploit, ghidra, ...)
      --flatpak   flatpak + Flathub runtime (apps later via kimrity-flatpak)

  Contents of /root:
      install.sh     installer (12 steps, with guards)
      dotfiles/      Hyprland, kitty, waybar, bash_profile
      hardening/     auditd rules, sysctl, sshd
      tools/         BlackArch arsenal lists + repo setup
      gate/          Security Gate CLI (scanner configs)
      kimai/ kimlogpipe/  broker + live log pipeline (installed by step 12)
      systemd/       user units + /etc audit watches
      kimscanning/   kimscan engine + en.yaml rules
      lab/           artifact #1 (SSH brute-force rule + report + evidence)

  Installed by install.sh into /usr/local/bin: kimrity-gate, kimscan.

  After installing: set your own passwords, then reboot.

  After install: `kimscan posture` checks the machine itself
  (SUPER + SHIFT + K on the desktop).
